SCOPE OF DERIVATION
-------------------
All of atlas-web is derived from Colibri `web/` (upstream 9d5d05de7f, v1.12.0)
EXCEPT the hydra-original files listed below. This includes files that match
upstream byte-for-byte (e.g. src/Brio.tsx, src/ErrorBoundary.tsx,
src/components/ui/{badge,button,input,textarea}.tsx, src/lib/{cortex,runtime,
storage,utils,brain-topics}.ts, src/brain-design.css, src/chat-design.css,
public/colibri-icon.svg, public/fonts/*) and files adapted from upstream
(everything under src/ not listed as hydra-original, plus vite.config.ts,
tsconfig*.json). src/lib/reasoning.ts matches upstream's pre-1.12.0
web/src/lib/reasoning.ts byte-for-byte (upstream deleted the file in the
1.12.0 redesign); it remains Colibri-derived.

HYDRA-ORIGINAL FILES (not derived from Colibri)
-----------------------------------------------
  server/server.ts          hydra atlas aggregation service + engine proxy
  scripts/proxy-smoke.ts    B4 allowlist smoke test
  src/Galaxy.tsx            3-D expert galaxy (hydra #787.4)
  public/favicon.svg
  README.md                 hydra deployment/ops documentation
  package.json              hydra scripts + dependency pinning
  LICENSE-colibri           verbatim copy of upstream LICENSE (this attribution)
  NOTICE                    this file

MODIFIED
--------
The derived files listed above are modified for integration into the
hydra_vortex atlas-web service: wiring to the hydra engine proxy
(/engine-proxy/<id>/...), the mock EMAP adapter, i18n additions, hydra
health/tier surfaces, and surfacing of /experts.json atlas failures instead
of silent degradation. They are NOT verbatim copies.

Third-party components bundled by upstream are listed in upstream's
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md; the fonts carried into public/fonts/ remain under
their own licenses (OFL.txt for bytesized, SIL Open Font License 1.1).
